Licence compatibility — verified 2026-09-11
-------------------------------------------

All three upstreams are LGPL-2.1. Section 3 of the LGPL-2.1 permits a licensee
to "opt to apply the terms of the ordinary GNU General Public License instead
of this License" to a given copy, choosing GPL version 2 "or any later
version". Farrer Park exercises that option and is distributed as GPL-3.0-only,
consistent with the rest of this workspace.

THE FLOW IS ONE-WAY. Code may be taken from these LGPL-2.1 upstreams into this
GPL-3.0-only crate; code from this crate CANNOT be contributed back to MOOSE or
the PRISMS codes under their LGPL-2.1 terms. This mirrors the situation
recorded for `raffles` (Apache-2.0 RAVEN into GPL-3.0) and for
`outram-park-fork-pflotran` (LGPL-2.1 PFLOTRAN into GPL-3.0).

Each licence was read from the upstream repository's own LICENSE file on
2026-09-11, not inferred from a badge, a package index, or prior belief.


Per-file attribution
--------------------

Any file that ports logic from one of the upstreams above MUST carry an
attribution header block naming the upstream project, the source file, the
version or commit it was read at, the copyright holder and the licence. Do not
strip those headers during refactors. A module that reimplements a documented
method from the open literature rather than from upstream source should say so
and cite the reference instead.


